Mistri's architecture is informed by pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono),
the agent harness by Mario Zechner, MIT licensed:
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
The ranking in lib/mistri/tool_search.rb follows pi's tool search.

Mistri also draws on lessons from truffle-rb, an earlier Ruby port of pi by the
same author as Mistri.

Parts of Mistri's MCP sign-in are adapted from the Model Context Protocol Ruby
SDK (https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/ruby-sdk), licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0):
the rules for application_type and for the address of a client ID metadata
document in lib/mistri/mcp/oauth/client_identity.rb, the rule for a resource
that covers a path in lib/mistri/mcp/oauth/tolerance.rb, and the cases for
them and for the issuer of a callback in test/test_mcp_oauth_checks.rb. The
rules were rewritten for Mistri's own sign-in calls, which take no class of
the SDK.
